# Follow-up to 2026-10-02-8.play: that run's rogue:assassination died at
# fightTime=47 under `mash` on flags and read alive:false, bar:locked clean
# through fightTime=105 -- 58 seconds dead, well past the ~10s clean revival
# (RESPAWN_EARLY=6/RESPAWN_LATE=11) this file's own "Tried and dropped"
# section already established for chained `play` calls. That section's own
# diagnosis is that a chained `play` gives up the instant hero()===null and
# never polls again, producing exactly this kind of stuck-looking read; the
# fix it names is one short `play` to get the death, then bare `wait`/`state`
# polling with no further `play` call. This settles which one happened here.
open
tap battleground
tap map:flags
tap class:rogue:assassination
tap pull
waitscreen fight 15

play mash 60
state
shot died

wait 5
state
shot plus5

wait 5
state
shot plus10

wait 5
state
shot plus15

wait 10
state
shot plus25
